#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
shadowfetch-welcome - first-boot welcome & setup for Shadowfetch Linux (Umbra).

A small, focused PyQt6 wizard that:
  - Opens with Ignition Setup: pick your flame (Core / Creator / Developer /
    AI Workstation / Full Flame) - mandatory first page until a choice is
    stamped, with honest measured sizes, an "already on your system" strip,
    an offline save-your-choice path, and automatic Phoenix Point protection
    around every install
  - Welcomes the user to Shadowfetch Linux
  - Opens Shadowfetch Guide for a private pre-install System Passport
  - Lets them choose a role-based setup profile to preselect useful apps
  - Lets them pick a signature accent colour (applied to KDE Plasma 6)
  - Offers a curated set of optional apps to install from Flathub
  - Offers Buzz; Buzz ranks and downloads open models in its Compute settings
  - Offers verified, user-level installs of Codex, Claude Code, Grok Build,
    and Cursor Agent
  - Offers the one-click software catalog (media apps, presets, local AI)

Honest, fast, private, AI-ready - built on Debian + KDE Plasma 6.
Everything here is reliable on Plasma 6; nothing is left half-working.
Zero telemetry: the only network activity is apt talking to the pinned
mirrors and downloads the user starts by clicking a card.
"""

